% Chapter 5
\chapter{Differential and Integrated Fiducial Cross Sections for Z Boson Production in the Four-Lepton dDecay Channel} \label{Chapter5} 
\chaptermark{Fiducial cross sections for $pp\rightarrow Z \rightarrow  4\ell$}
 The process $pp \rightarrow Z \rightarrow 4\ell$ is significantly important for calibrating and validating $\HZZllll$ process. 
 Figure~\ref{fig:mass4l} shows clear $Z \rightarrow 4\ell$ resonance of at four-lepton invariant mass $m_{4\ell} = m_Z$ which act as a standard
 candle for $H \rightarrow 4\ell$. The measurement of $Z \rightarrow 4\ell$ fiducial cross section is important to test SM theoretical prediction
 and to validate Higgs measurements methodology. The inclusive and differential fiducial cross sections of $Z \rightarrow 4\ell$ have been performed 
 on the footings of Higgs measurements, using same differential variables using  8~TeV  data. The inclusive
 Z boson production cross section measurement using $Z \rightarrow 4\ell$ decay channel at 7~TeV has already been measured in Ref.~\cite{Z4LPaper}.
 The inclusive ratio of $H\rightarrow4\ell$ and $Z\rightarrow4\ell$ fiducial cross section is also reported using 8~TeV data. 
 The motivation for the ratio is to cancel out fraction of  systematic uncertainties and to validate Higgs measurements. 
 \section{Extraction of Inclusive and Differential Fiducial Cross Sections for \texorpdfstring{$\Zllll$}{Z to 4l}}\label{sec:ExtractionZ4l_indep}}
 The $Z\rightarrow4\ell$ fiducial cross section measurements are extracted in $m_{4\ell}$ range from 50 to 105~GeV. 
 In part of the $m_{4\ell}$ spectrum below 100~GeV, the dominant contribution is coming from the resonant $Z\rightarrow4\ell$ decays
 (s-channel of the $\Pq\Paq \to \Z\gamma^{*} \to 4\ell$ process). The sub-dominant contributions arise from the corresponding
 t- and u-channels in the $\Pq\Paq \to \Z\gamma^{*} \to 4\ell$ process, from the reducible
 background processes (Z+X), as well as from the $\Pg\Pg \to \Z\Z$ background. In case of the $Z\rightarrow4\ell$ measurements, the s-channel
 of the $\Pq\Paq \to \Z\gamma^{*} \to 4\ell$ process is considered as signal, while the other processes are considered as backgrounds. Contributions 
 from s-, t- and u-channels in  the $\Pq\Paq \to \Z\Z \to 4\ell$ process (and their interference), as well as the $\Pg\Pg \to \Z\Z$ process are 
 estimated from Monte Carlo simulations, while $\Z+X$ background is estimated from data. 
 For $Z \rightarrow 4\ell$ cross-section measurements,  the MC samples for the the process $\Pq\Paq(\to \Z\Z^*)\to 4\ell$ have  been produced 
 using {\sc powheg} generator with separate contributions of t- and u-channels of the process.
  \par
 For $\Zllll$ fiducial cross section measurements, fiducial volume definition and statistical prescription are similar to the ones performed 
 for the $\Hllll$ fiducial cross section measurements described in Sections~\ref{sec:ExtractionInclusive} and \ref{sec:ExtractionDifferential}, 
 while mass of Z boson is fixed to PDG value of $m_Z = 91.18$~GeV~\cite{PDG_14}. The procedure for the extraction of the cross sections differ in only three aspects. 
 First, the acceptance four-lepton invariant mass window is changed
 to $50 < m_{4\ell} < 105$~GeV. Second, the functional form of the $m_{4\ell}$ spectra of the $\Zllll$ decays is adopted to the $\Zllll$ resonance. 
 Third, in case of the $\Zllll$ measurements, we do not have the wrong combination contribution as in case of the $\Hllll$ measurements
 (e.g. characteristic for the ZH, WH, and ttH production modes), and we do not need to extract it in the fit  separately. Backgrounds are extracted 
 following the procedure described in Section~\ref{sec:EventsBackgrounds}.
 \par 
 The expected number of events arising from all these processes, and number of observed candidates after final selection in data in the mass 
 region $50 < m_{4\ell} < 105 \GeV$) are given in  Table~\ref{tab:EventYieldsZ4l}, for 2012 (8\TeV) data-taking period.  The $Z\rightarrow 4l $ peak in 
 the $m_{4\ell}$ spectra is modelled with a Relativistic Breit-Wigner function convoluted with a Crystal Ball function
 (single-sided instead of double-sided as the case for $H\rightarrow 4l$). The exact functional form is given by the equations:

\begin{eqnarray}
f_{BW}(m_{4l}|m_{Z}) & = & N\cdot \frac{2}{\pi} \cdot \frac{\Gamma_{Z}^2 m_{Z}^2}{(m_{4l}^2-m_{Z}^2)^2 + m_{4l}^4\cdot(\Gamma_{Z}^2/m_{Z}^2)}
\end{eqnarray}

\begin{equation}
CB(\xi) = N \cdot \left\{
  \begin{array}{lr}
      A \cdot (B+|\xi|)^{-n_L} , ~{\rm for}~\xi < \alpha_L \\
      exp(-\xi^2/2), ~{\rm for}~\xi >= \alpha_L \\
  \end{array}
\right.
\end{equation}

\begin{eqnarray}
f(m_{4l}|m_{Z}) &=& CB(m_{Z}^{'}) \otimes f_{BW}(m_{4l}|m_{Z})
\end{eqnarray}
\par
In this functional form, the mass width of the Z boson is set to the world average value ($\Gamma_{Z}=2.4952$~GeV)~\cite{PDG_14}, $m_{4l}$ is variable, while $m_Z$ is
the Z mass peak position. The resulting fits of the $Z\rightarrow 4l $ signal shape are shown on Figure~\ref{fig:mass_pdf_z4l}.
