\subsubsection{Extraction of the Ratio of $\Hllll$ and $\Zllll$ fiducial Cross Sections} \label{sec:ExtractionZ4l_ratio}

A simultaneous fit for the $\Hllll$ and $\Zllll$ signal peaks has also been preformed in order to measure the ratio of $\Hllll$ and $\Zllll$ fiducial
cross sections. This measurement is performed in a mass range $50 < m(4l) < 140$~GeV, by generalizing the procedure to include both resonances. The measurement
is based on the same signal models of $\Hllll$ and $\Zllll$ as presented in Sections~\ref{sec:ExtractionInclusive} and~\ref{sec:ExtractionZ4l_indep} 
respectively. The results are extracted simultaneously for $H\rightarrow4\ell$ and the ratio of the  $H\rightarrow4\ell$ and $Z\rightarrow4\ell$. The measurements
have been performed in two scenario. In the first scenario, the measurement is extracted by fixing the mass of Z boson to PDG value and Higgs mass
to $m_H = 125$~GeV. In the second  scenario,  the masses of both resonance are allowed to float and fit for difference of masses of both resonances
$\Delta m = m_H - m_Z$ and the Higgs boson $m_H$. This scenario helps to reduce the systematic uncertainty due to lepton momentum scale resolution and provide
an extra validation for methodology of the measurements.
\par 
The number of estimated background and signal events, and number of observed candidates after inclusive selection
in the range $50 < m_{4l} < 140$~GeV, which is used for measurement of the ratio of $\Hllll$ and $\Zllll$ fiducial cross-sections, is shown
in Table~\ref{tab:EventYieldsRatio}.


